WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:19.502
The Lemonade Detectives watched as Robby stomped away without another word.

2
00:00:19.503 --> 00:00:23.697
"What's wrong with him?" Cole asked, still staring after Robby.

3
00:00:23.698 --> 00:00:29.508
Henry was wondering the same thing. Robby's behavior seemed suspicious.

4
00:00:29.509 --> 00:00:34.834
"Why is Robby so mad at Mr. Tate?" he asked one of the other kids.

5
00:00:34.835 --> 00:00:37.467
"I don't know," the kid said.

6
00:00:37.468 --> 00:00:42.207
"Anyway, I think I hear my mom calling me." He ran off.

7
00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:47.815
Henry looked at another kid. "Why's everybody acting so weird?" he asked him.

8
00:00:47.816 --> 00:00:50.756
"Is it because of what Robby said?"

9
00:00:50.757 --> 00:00:54.463
"No. Maybe. I mean, I have to go too."

10
00:00:54.464 --> 00:00:58.457
The second kid scooped up the ball and hurried away.

11
00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:02.178
Two others left after him, leaving only Emma.

12
00:01:02.179 --> 00:01:07.984
"What's going on?" Maggie asked Emma. "Why did Robby get so angry just now?

13
00:01:07.985 --> 00:01:12.152
Does he really want Mr. Tate to leave West Belltown?"

14
00:01:12.153 --> 00:01:15.763
"I guess," Emma said in a soft voice.

15
00:01:15.764 --> 00:01:18.489
"But why?" Cole asked.

16
00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:22.307
"I think it would be cool to have a new ice-cream place in my neighborhood!"

17
00:01:22.308 --> 00:01:28.453
Emma shrugged. "I'm not sure. But I should go home too," she said.

18
00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:32.335
"I told my dad I'd help him give our dog a bath."

19
00:01:32.336 --> 00:01:35.318
She said good-bye and hurried away.

20
00:01:35.319 --> 00:01:38.887
"That was weird," Cole said when she was gone.

21
00:01:38.888 --> 00:01:42.668
"Robby seemed really angry when we mentioned Mr. Tate."

22
00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:47.395
"Yeah. He always seems pretty happy at school," Henry said.

23
00:01:47.396 --> 00:01:50.992
"Maybe he should be our first suspect."

24
00:01:50.993 --> 00:01:55.281
"Do you think Robby stole Mr. Tate's ice cream?" Maggie asked.

25
00:01:55.282 --> 00:01:57.356
"Why would he do that?"

26
00:01:57.357 --> 00:02:02.597
"All those kids were acting weird just now, not just Robby," Henry said.

27
00:02:02.598 --> 00:02:04.807
"Any of them could have done it."

28
00:02:04.808 --> 00:02:07.270
Maggie looked doubtful.

29
00:02:07.271 --> 00:02:13.093
"You think one of those kids broke into the Dessert Den and carried off all Mr. Tate's ice cream?"

30
00:02:13.094 --> 00:02:18.192
"Maybe they didn't carry it off." Cole grinned. "Maybe they ate it!"

31
00:02:18.193 --> 00:02:23.196
"Mr. Tate didn't say his ice cream was stolen," Henry reminded them.

32
00:02:23.197 --> 00:02:27.319
"He said his ice-cream flavor was stolen."

33
00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.436
"What does that mean?" Maggie looked confused.

34
00:02:30.437 --> 00:02:33.120
"How can someone steal a flavor?"

35
00:02:33.121 --> 00:02:38.424
"I don't know," Henry said. "Let's ask Mr. Tate when we see him.

36
00:02:38.425 --> 00:02:43.032
We need to find out exactly what happened."

37
00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:46.384
They walked their bikes the rest of the way to the Dessert Den.

38
00:02:46.385 --> 00:02:52.869
As they got closer, Henry saw a plumber leaving the shop.

39
00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:58.875
"Wow," Cole said, peering inside the front door. "This place looks cool!"

40
00:02:58.876 --> 00:03:04.940
Henry nodded. The Dessert Den had big glass windows and a fancy sign out front.

41
00:03:04.941 --> 00:03:12.352
Inside, tables and chairs were painted in bright colors, and there were bins filled with candy and other treats.

42
00:03:12.353 --> 00:03:17.016
The front door was locked, but Henry could see Mr. Tate inside.

43
00:03:17.017 --> 00:03:21.727
He was sweeping the floor in the dining area. Maggie knocked on the door.

44
00:03:21.728 --> 00:03:27.471
Mr. Tate looked up and then came over to unlock the door.

45
00:03:27.472 --> 00:03:32.481
"Hello," he greeted them. He sounded a lot more cheerful than he had earlier.

46
00:03:32.482 --> 00:03:34.660
"You're just in time."

47
00:03:34.661 --> 00:03:39.045
"Just in time for what?" Cole asked as he walked inside with the others.

48
00:03:39.046 --> 00:03:40.906
"Did you solve the mystery?"

49
00:03:40.907 --> 00:03:46.653
"No, nothing like that." Mr. Tate hurried over to the shiny, tiled counter.

50
00:03:46.654 --> 00:03:49.319
Several white boxes were sitting there.

51
00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:56.661
"I just got a very special delivery—some of the caramel-swirl brownies I'll be selling. Want a taste?"

52
00:03:56.662 --> 00:04:01.099
"Sure!" Cole said eagerly. "I love brownies!"

53
00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:04.935
"You love every kind of dessert," Maggie reminded him.

54
00:04:04.936 --> 00:04:10.738
Mr. Tate chuckled. "Great! You're my perfect customer."

55
00:04:10.739 --> 00:04:14.946
He opened one of the boxes and handed each of the kids a brownie.

56
00:04:14.947 --> 00:04:23.300
Henry tasted his. "Yum! This is delicious!" he said. Cole and Maggie agreed.

57
00:04:23.301 --> 00:04:26.746
"I'm glad you like it," Mr. Tate said, smiling.

58
00:04:26.747 --> 00:04:30.390
"Tell all your friends to come to my grand opening tomorrow, okay?"

59
00:04:30.391 --> 00:04:33.467
"Sure." Cole licked his fingers.

60
00:04:33.468 --> 00:04:37.139
"But first, maybe you should tell us more about your mystery."

61
00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:42.893
Mr. Tate's smile faded. He glanced at a menu that was hanging above the counter.

62
00:04:42.894 --> 00:04:47.744
Henry could only see part of the menu. The rest was covered with a sheet.

63
00:04:47.745 --> 00:04:52.875
"You said someone stole your new ice-cream flavor," Henry reminded him.

64
00:04:52.876 --> 00:04:55.432
"What does that mean?"

65
00:04:55.433 --> 00:05:00.003
"The Dessert Den is going to serve all kinds of desserts," Mr. Tate said.

66
00:05:00.004 --> 00:05:02.666
"But one of our specialties is ice cream.

67
00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:06.891
So I invented a brand-new, exclusive flavor for my grand opening.

68
00:05:06.892 --> 00:05:09.038
It's supposed to be top secret.

69
00:05:09.039 --> 00:05:13.521
But somehow, someone found out about it—and stole it!"

70
00:05:13.522 --> 00:05:17.719
"How does someone steal a flavor?" Maggie wondered.

71
00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:21.582
"And who would do something like that, anyway?" Cole added.

72
00:05:21.583 --> 00:05:25.048
"I know exactly who stole it!" Mr. Tate snapped.

73
00:05:25.049 --> 00:05:27.847
"I just need you kids to help me prove it!"

74
00:05:27.848 --> 00:05:30.582
Henry felt more confused than ever.

75
00:05:30.583 --> 00:05:36.136
"You already know who stole your flavor?" he said. "Who?"

76
00:05:36.137 --> 00:05:44.140
Mr. Tate scowled. "It was Mrs. Sweet, who owns the Sweet Shop!"
